# Steps for SQLA Generation

Install and activate the project

```bash
poetry install
poetry env activate
```

```bash
# delete the old revision test
rm versions/revision_test.py

gen-sqla src/analysis_api_schema/schema/analysis_api_schema.yaml > migrations/schema.py

# On windows, Powershell will save as UTF-16LE 🤮 you can run this, or open and re-save with UTF-8
Get-Content -Path "migrations/schema.py" | Set-Content -Path "migrations/schema.py" -Encoding UTF8

# generate the migration
alembic revision --autogenerate --rev-id="revision" -m "test"
```

# LinkML Dumping

```bash
schemauto.exe import-sql postgresql+psycopg2://developer:developer@localhost:5432/emsl1000soils > schema.yml
```

> NOTE! Many features of the Postgres DB _like UUID's_ are not captured by schemauto yet. **Don't rely on schemauto alone!**



Generic single-database configuration.

# Migration Commands

```
Usage: flask db [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Perform database migrations.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  branches   Show current branch points
  current    Display the current revision for each database.
  downgrade  Revert to a previous version
  edit       Edit a revision file
  heads      Show current available heads in the script directory
  history    List changeset scripts in chronological order.
  init       Creates a new migration repository.
  merge      Merge two revisions together, creating a new revision file
  migrate    Autogenerate a new revision file (Alias for 'revision...
  revision   Create a new revision file.
  show       Show the revision denoted by the given symbol.
  stamp      'stamp' the revision table with the given revision; don't...
  upgrade    Upgrade to a later version
```



```bash
flask db migrate -m "Migration Message"

flask db upgrade

flask db downgrade
```

Look for `INFO  [alembic.env] No changes in schema detected.` in case no changes are detected.
No migration file will be generated.

# pip changes

```bash
pip install psycopg2-binary
pip install --upgrade alembic
pip install ruff

pip install -e .
```

